This was my second ascension (First was a samurai in 3.2.2).
Played on  http://alt.org/nethack , starting on September 7th.


The dungeon seemed to have a definite lack when it came to magic
lamps, as not a single one was to be seen, and only got wishes in
the castle.  Paxed started out with a magic marker, but that wasn't
really needed as in the end he had 5 magic markers, only 2 of which
he used.


I decided to play him with protection racket in mind, and thanks to
a splint mail found on the 2nd dlvl, this became slightly more probable
to succeed.  On the same level, there was a tiny general store, where
paxed found a scroll costing only 26 zorkmids, and a smoky potion.

On dlvl 3 a shopkeeper named Zonguldak kept his armoury, and there
paxed bought a shiny silvery shield.  Unfortunately, all this heavy
stuff was making paxed burdened, so he decided to use up some of the
potions;  Quaffing the smoky potion, out poured a djinni, but it seemed
to be in too much of a hurry to grant a wish.

On dlvl 4 paxed found the entrance to the mines, and as the gnomes and
dwarves there hailed him as a friend, there was no need to be overly careful.
The first level of mines started out nicely, but then, the little cat Mirri
stepped on a level teleporter, and I doubted whether paxed could make it to
the minetown.  Luckily, on the same level he found a real diamond, so cash
wasn't going to be a problem, and the pick-axe provided a quick way down
to the minetown.

I later found Mirri, still tame.

The minetown altar was Quetzalcoatl's, but sacrificing wasn't on his mind;
instead paxed went and sold his diamond and a citrine stone, and bought
protection.  With AC -6, paxed felt he was ready to take on the world.

...

I encountered 3 bones files in this game, one the level below minetown,
the other two bit deeper in the DoD.
The game before the castle I wore the armor I had during the mines, and used
Excalibur i had found on a bones pile.  Portal to the quest was on dlvl 14,
in a small room with an altar.  Luring all the wolves and snakes near the
portal and the lugging the corpses on the God's BBQ grill resulted in
Quetzalcoatl throwing me Grayswandir, which I used from then on.

I met an arch-lich on the Medusa's, and I had no magic protection, so I
blessed genocided L after that one destroyed my speed boots.

Coming back up from the Medusa's (I had no means of blinding myself),
digging straight tunnels between stairs, I accidentally found the entrance
to Fort Ludios, and coming out of there I was carrying well over 100k gold,
which I later decided to donate to the minetown priest.
I wanted to get clairvoyance, but accidentally typoed while donating, and
ended up giving most of my gold in one shot.

Somewhere after getting Grayswandir my cat polymorphed into a red dragon,
and I kept him until he died biting a blue jelly in Fort Ludios.

Next up: castle.
Got a wish from the castle throne, which I used for speed boots, and
#sitting again gave an identify, but all I had for that was the boots I had
just gotten.  Very handy. =)  The castle wand was at 2 charges.

After scouring most of the dungeons for scrolls, potions and tools,
I polypiled in Ludios until I was blue in the face, and after that I was
pretty much kitted to ascend.  (I wished for the one and only wand of
polymorph in this game)

I wasn't ready to do the quest until after this polypiling session, but
then the Minion of Huhetotl crumbled like tissue paper...

Coming back up after grabbing the Amulet wasn't too hard, got thrown back
only once, and had to slug through Juiblex's swamp again, and Rodney
did his appearance 3 or 4 times all together, but he didn't have time to
double trouble or steal.

Used the confused gold detection trick on all planes, and even Water was
surprisingly easy, i practically stumbled on the portal.
To stay unburdened, I dumped the Book in Moloch's Sanctum, the Bell
on Air, and the Candelabrum on Fire.

The 3rd altar was the correct one.  Unfortunately my guardian angel had
died sometime earlier.


Most memorable moment:  The first thing Orcus did when he woke up was to
summon Demo, and I wasn't mentally quite prepared to face him.  Orcus died
easily, but Demo was a bit harder.
Got a wonderful adrenaline rush from that  =)


